{
  "info": {
    "name": "BusinessCard4U API",
    "description": "BusinessCard4U API - Laravel 12 + Sanctum.\n\nSETUP\n1. Start the API so your phone/other devices can reach it:\n     cd business_card\n     php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8001\n2. Set the {{base_url}} collection variable to your PC's current LAN IP.\n   It is DHCP, so re-check with ipconfig after a reconnect or reboot.\n\nHAPPY PATH ORDER\n  Send OTP -> Verify OTP -> Complete Register   (or just Login)\n  Create Company -> Create Business Card -> Update / Search / Scan QR\n\nAUTO-CAPTURED VARIABLES\n  token             <- Login / Complete Register / Refresh Token\n  otp               <- Send OTP (only when APP_ENV=local)\n  company_id        <- Create Company\n  business_card_id  <- Create Business Card\n  qr_code_data      <- Create Business Card (used by Scan QR)\n  friend_card_id    <- Search Business Cards (first result)\n\nNOTES\n- Update Business Card is POST + _method=PUT on purpose. PHP does not populate\n  the request body or $_FILES for a multipart PUT, so a real PUT updates nothing.\n- Addresses are structured: city and country are required per entry.\n- Logging in deletes every existing token for that user, so only one device can\n  be signed in at a time.\n- forgot-password / reset-password / change-password / refresh-token work on the\n  API but are not wired to any screen in the Flutter app yet.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://192.168.99.200:8001/api"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "testuser@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "password123"
    },
    {
      "key": "otp",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "reset_token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "company_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "business_card_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "friend_card_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "qr_code_data",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth - Public",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/send-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "send-otp"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (json.otp) {",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('otp', json.otp);",
                  "        console.log('OTP captured (local env only):', json.otp);",
                  "    }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP",
